{"kind": "report", "step": 18, "ts": "2026-11-18T04:17:03.868479+00:00", "data": {"category": "wan", "host": "external", "component": "modem", "cause": "The internet dropped because the cable modem lost sync with the ISP plant at 02:01:44 (No Ranging Response / T3 time-out, then TFTP config file NOT FOUND) and only re-registered at 02:28:21, while the firewall's WAN session stayed stale because the watchdog runs in observe mode and never applied its logged reload.", "evidence": ["ping -c 3 -n 198.51.100.1 -> 3 transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss: ISP gateway unreachable though the link is up", "arp -n -> ARP entry for 198.51.100.1 (00:17:10:9a:a3:96) present, so the local LAN-to-modem link is fine; the break is upstream", "ifconfig vtnet0 -> UP,RUNNING,LOWER_UP with inet 198.51.100.27; netstat -rn -> default route via 198.51.100.1 \u2014 firewall NIC and routing are healthy", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-events.jsonl -> 02:01:44 'No Ranging Response received - T3 time-out', 02:14:10 'TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND', 02:28:21 'Cable Modem Reboot ... registration complete'", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-metrics.jsonl -> NOT_SYNCHRONIZED at 02:06, OPERATIONAL by 02:29-02:40 with uncorrected codewords 112->131 and ~52k corrected blocks (degraded plant)", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/events.jsonl + state.json -> outage_start 02:06, decisions 'none' while modem not_operational/settling, then 'would_reload' at 02:30 and 02:40 in observe mode \u2014 nothing was applied", "cat /var/db/dhclient.leases.vtnet0 -> lease unchanged (198.51.100.27, server-identifier 203.0.113.67) across the modem reboot, i.e. stale WAN session"], "action": "contact_provider", "recommendation": "The wan_reload fix was requested and its preconditions were met (in this drill nothing was actually changed). Operationally: reconfigure/renew the WAN on gw.lan so it re-negotiates against the now-OPERATIONAL modem, take the watchdog out of observe mode so its logged reload actually executes, and report the T3 time-out / missing TFTP configuration file to the ISP, since the trigger was on their plant/provisioning side.", "detail": "Modem lost cable-plant sync (T3 timeout, TFTP config NOT FOUND); WAN session never refreshed because watchdog is observe-only", "contributing": {"host": "gw.lan", "component": "monitoring_config"}}}
